module

public import WeilConjectures.AlgebraicGeometry.NormalizedBlowup
public import Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.FiniteType
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.IntegralClosure.IntegrallyClosed
public import WeilConjectures.Mathlib.AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheaf.Invertible

/-!
# Mapping property of normalized blowups

Source: Illusie--Laszlo--Orgogozo, Travaux de Gabber, Expose VIII, 2.2.2 and
Proposition 2.2.4(i), printed p.90; Stacks Project, Tags 0806 and 035Q(4)
(blueprint: lem-trf-normalized-blowup-finality).
-/

@[expose] public section

set_option autoImplicit false

universe u

open CategoryTheory

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData

/-- The normalized blowup is normal, maximally dominating, and principalizes its centre;
it is final for maximally dominating maps from arbitrary normal schemes on which the
extended centre is an effective Cartier ideal. Since S is finite type over Q, it is
Noetherian, so coherence of the quasi-coherent ideal means finite generation on affine opens.
The dense open complement meets each irreducible component densely, since S has finitely
many irreducible components. No finiteness condition is imposed on Y.

Source: ILO, Expose VIII, 2.2.2 and Proposition 2.2.4(i), printed p.90;
Stacks Project, Tags 0806 and 035Q(4)
(blueprint: lem-trf-normalized-blowup-finality).

Proof:
1. Put U = S minus V(J), B = Bl_J(S), and N = B^nu. By
lem-trf-reduced-blowup-generic-geometry, B is reduced and locally Noetherian with finitely
many irreducible components, the blowup is an isomorphism above U, and it bijects generic
points. Apply lem-sfb-componentwise-normalization-generic-properties to B. Its normalization
is normal and takes generic points to generic points; composing gives that property for p.
2. By thm-nagata-blowup-principalizes-center, J O_B is locally generated by a regular a.
On an affine chart Spec A with this generator, lem-sfb-normalization-affine-total-fractions
identifies its normalized inverse image with Spec of the integral closure of A in Q(A).
The element a is a unit of Q(A), hence is still a nonzerodivisor on that subring.
Extension of ideals composes, so J O_N is generated by this same a on these charts.
This proves invertibility without assuming normalization flat.
3. For the given Y and f, thm-nagata-blowup-universal-property gives a unique g : Y -> B
over S because J O_Y is invertible. Each generic point of Y maps into U, to a generic
point of S. The isomorphism over U and the generic-point bijection imply that g takes
this point to a generic point of B. Continuity then shows that each component of Y
dominates the corresponding component of B.
4. Apply lem-sfb-component-dominant-normalization-lift to g. The target condition holds
because B has finitely many components. The source condition is exactly normality of Y,
with no quasi-compactness or local Noetherianity requirement. The resulting unique lift
h : Y -> N has composite f with p.
5. Any two lifts over S have equal composites to B by blowup uniqueness. Normalization
uniqueness applied to this common g then identifies the lifts. The argument includes
empty Y and empty S; the unit ideal gives the normalization mapping property. -/
theorem normalizedBlowup_finality (S : Scheme.{u})
    (q : S ⟶ Spec (.of (ULift.{u} ℚ))) [IsReduced S]
    [LocallyOfFiniteType q] [QuasiCompact q] (J : S.IdealSheafData)
    (hJ : ∀ U : S.affineOpens, (J.ideal U).FG)
    (hcentre : Dense (J.support.compl : Set S)) :
    (∀ x : J.normalizedBlowup,
      IsDomain (J.normalizedBlowup.presheaf.stalk x) ∧
      IsIntegrallyClosed (J.normalizedBlowup.presheaf.stalk x)) ∧
    Set.MapsTo J.normalizedBlowupMap (genericPoints J.normalizedBlowup) (genericPoints S) ∧
    (J.comap J.normalizedBlowupMap).IsInvertible ∧
    (∀ (Y : Scheme.{u}) (f : Y ⟶ S),
      (∀ y : Y, IsDomain (Y.presheaf.stalk y) ∧
        IsIntegrallyClosed (Y.presheaf.stalk y)) →
      Set.MapsTo f (genericPoints Y) (genericPoints S) → (J.comap f).IsInvertible →
      ∃! l : Y ⟶ J.normalizedBlowup, l ≫ J.normalizedBlowupMap = f) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData
